  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Thursday...\n\nScattered showers (20-60% chance) will continue this afternoon and\nevening and a few (5-20% chance) embedded thunderstorms may\ndevelop. With these showers, wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph have been\nobserved. These showers will also have occasional pockets of heavy\nrain. Over the far southeastern corner of Montana and much of \nWyoming, a strong to severe storm or two may develop late \nafternoon/early evening with strong wind gusts of 60+ mph as the \nmain threat. Isolated showers (10-40% chance) will linger \novernight into Saturday morning.\n\nSaturday will see a similar setup to today as an upper level\ntrough continues to approach. There is better potential for strong\nto severe thunderstorms to develop across Wyoming and southern\nMontana as CAPE values will be around 600-1400 J/kg and shear will\nbe around 30-45 kts. The main threats with these storms will be\nstrong wind gusts, large hail, and pockets of heavy rain.\n\nOn Sunday the trough moves east across the region, exiting early\nMonday, and bringing a widespread 40-70% chance for showers and\nthunderstorms. Strong subsidence will bring a brief period of dry\nand breezy conditions behind the front late Sunday.\n\nBrief ridging builds in Monday into midweek. Conditions are \nexpected to be mostly dry Monday, but weak shortwaves in the flow \nwill allow a low chance (10-30%) for showers and thunderstorms \nTuesday and Wednesday. Temperatures will also warm slightly\nduring this time. By late Wednesday, upper level flow begins to \nturn out of the southwest, allowing temperatures to cool toward\nthe end of the week and continuing the chance (20-40%) of \nafternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms.\n\nTemperatures will cool into Sunday, with highs falling to low 70s\nto low 80s. Temperatures then warm into the middle of the week,\nwith highs in the 80s to low 90s by Wednesday. Then, temperatures\ntrend towards seasonal for the end of the week (low 80s). Archer",
